  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.TitleAdd">Add remote device</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.Name">Name (your choice)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.AddressHint">Host and port, for example 192.168.1.42:22000. Without a port, 22000 is assumed. If you leave this empty, discovery is asked for the device’s current address on every connect.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.DeviceId">Remote device ID</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.IdHint">In the remote device’s Syncthing UI under “This Device → Identification”.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.AutoConnect">Connect automatically at startup</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.Discovery">Look up the address on the discovery server</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.Relay">Connect through a relay when there is no direct route</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.RelayHint">Both are needed for a remote device with no port open to the outside. A relay routes the connection through someone else’s machine and is slower than any direct connection. It is used only when no direct connection can be established.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.Address">Address</s:String>

  <s:String x:Key="S.Peers.Hint">Syncthing requires both sides to know each other. A remote device must share its folders with this device explicitly. Only then do the shares appear in the list and can be connected.</s:String>
