  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.Conflict">On conflicts</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.KeepBoth">Keep both, rename the losing one</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.Newer">Newer file wins</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.Older">Older file wins</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.Local">Local file wins</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Conflict.Remote">Remote file wins</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.ConflictHint">A conflict arises when both sides have changed the same file. With renaming, both versions are kept; the losing one is named name.sync-conflict-20260302-193044-YWS4CCA.jpg, as in Syncthing. With every other setting the losing version is deleted.</s:String>

  <s:String x:Key="M.PreviewShort">{0} images, {1}</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.KeepVersions">Keep replaced versions</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.VersionsHint">When a file is replaced by the remote version or deleted at its request, the version held here moves to the folder “.stversions” inside the share. That folder takes no part in synchronisation. Placeholders without content are not kept, because there is nothing to save.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.VersionDays">Keep for days</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Share.VersionDaysHint">After this time a kept version is removed. Counting starts on the day it was put aside, not from its modification time.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S2.DaysInvalid">The retention time must be at least 1 day.</s:String>
